EXPERIMENT 60 – API TESTING OF WEATHER INFORMATION SERVICE USING APACHE JMETER
AIM
To use Apache JMeter to create test cases for API testing of a weather information service.
ALGORITHM
1. Start Apache JMeter and rename the Test Plan.
2. Add a Thread Group.
3. Set Threads = 5, Ramp-up = 5 seconds and Loop Count = 2.
4. Add HTTP Request Defaults for the weather API server.
5. Create Test Case 1 (valid input):
   - GET /v1/forecast
   - Add Response Assertion for code 200.
   - Add JSON Assertion for $.current_weather.temperature.
   - Add Duration Assertion of 2000 milliseconds.
6. Create Test Case 2 (invalid input):
   - GET /v1/forecast with latitude 999.
   - Add Response Assertion for code 400.
   - Select Ignore Status.
7. Add View Results Tree and Summary Report.
8. Run the test and verify the temperature value.
INPUT
Test Plan Configuration
Element	Property	Value
Thread Group	Threads	5
Thread Group	Ramp-up	5 seconds
Thread Group	Loop Count	2
HTTP Request Defaults	Protocol	https
HTTP Request Defaults	Server	api.open-meteo.com

Test Case 1 – Valid Location
Property	Value
Method	GET
Path	/v1/forecast
Latitude	13.08
Longitude	80.27
current_weather	true
Response Assertion	Code = 200
JSON Assertion	$.current_weather.temperature
Duration Assertion	2000 ms

Test Case 2 – Invalid Latitude
Property	Value
Method	GET
Path	/v1/forecast
Latitude	999
Longitude	80.27
current_weather	true
Response Assertion	Code = 400
Ignore Status	Selected

